WEBVTT

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.300
<i>The first time I met her, I knew instantly...</i>

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.050
<i>She must've been Kuro-kun's first love.</i>

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.910
She seems nice, Kuro.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:32.050
This is my girlfriend and my senpai 
in college, Yumihara Saki-san.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.880
I-It's nice to meet you!

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.010
Well, I'll be at the café downstairs.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:39.990
Huh?

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.560
I'd just be in the way here.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.260
I just wanted to say hello. 
So you can take your time, okay?

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:47.570
If you'll excuse me.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.150
<i>So she's Kuro-kun's...</i>

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.580
<i>But it seemed like she was</i>

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.110
<i>silently...</i>

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.210
<i>silently corrupting those around her.</i>

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.260
<i>That's how she seemed.</i>

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:11.390
I heard Sakuragawa-san was taken to 
the operating room again yesterday.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:14.270
Really? She tried to kill herself again?

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.320
Maybe the rumor that she's tried to 
kill herself multiple times is true.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.180
I heard she doesn't have long to live.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.980
She was tying you down.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:31.960
But if going out with Iwanaga-san 
will help you break free of that...

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.530
I think it's a good thing, 
despite feeling conflicted.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:44.160
Saki-san, I do love Rikka-san, 
and I might be tied down,

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.230
but I do sometimes wish she wasn't around.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.670
That she wasn't around? 
Didn't Rikka-san pass away?

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.390
Rikka-san hasn't passed away.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.630
That's not possible.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:05.220
Saki-san, Rikka-san is my cousin.

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:09.970
<i>Don't tell me she's also... a Sakuragawa.</i>

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:46.950
<i>I screwed up... I screwed up so bad.</i>

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:51.660
<i>How could I create time for Kuro-senpai 
and Saki-san to be alone together?!</i>

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.670
<i>What in the world happened? 
Why are things so awkward now?!</i>

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:57.110
Iwanaga.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.190
This would be a good time 
to replenish some nutrients.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:05.090
It's about time for 
Steel Lady Nanase to appear.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.170
If I'm here,

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:11.190
the ayakashi that come to tell you about 
Steel Lady Nanase might get scared.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:14.530
Saki-san, I'll be waiting by the exit.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:18.020
All right. Then I'll be in 
the car with Iwanaga-san.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:21.820
<i>Saki-san just had someone 
close to her get murdered,</i>

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.150
<i>and now she and Kuro-san, 
who's such a kind person...</i>

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:27.770
<i>They are a man and woman who 
planned to get married at one point.</i>

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.980
<i>I was asleep for about an hour and a half.</i>

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.420
<i>You could do a lot in an hour and a half...</i>

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:38.540
<i>And I mean a lot!</i>

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.510
Iwanaga-san.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.510
Have you ever met Rikka-san?

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.570
Yes, I have, but...

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:52.310
The hospital where Rikka-san was admitted 
was also where I was staying.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:57.810
I see. So you know that she also ate 
the flesh of a kudan and a mermaid.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.730
<i>Senpai mentioned that he 
hadn't told Saki-san about</i>

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.810
<i>Rikka-san's condition...</i>

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.530
<i>Is she trying to get me to spill something?</i>

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.680
<i>Oh, very well.</i>

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:13.000
I do, because Rikka-san was 
also feared by the monsters.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:17.040
Though she and Kuro-senpai 
haven't told me the details,

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.790
she was apparently hospitalized

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:22.300
long-term so that her body and 
abilities could be examined.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.420
<i>Is that what it was?</i>

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.790
How is she lately?

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:31.140
She was living in my mansion 
up until a month ago.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:32.360
What?

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:35.810
She was suddenly discharged 
at the beginning of the year.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:38.270
But why would she go to your house?

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:43.570
As his girlfriend, how could I possibly 
let her and Kuro-senpai live together?

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:48.040
Rikka-san was discharged 
due to the appointment of

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.590
a new hospital director and the 
resulting change in political climate.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:56.250
Because the hospital really didn't 
know what to do with her, either.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:06:00.010
I'm sure there were many who 
were happy to see her go.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.010
Sakuragawa Rikka-sama

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:06.610
And because of that, there were rumors 
that Rikka-san didn't have long to live.

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:10.990
So what do you say? How do you feel 
about leaving the hospital soon?

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.620
Do you really have to say it like that?

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.270
What if she resists?

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.070
Then she'll leave us no choice.

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:19.990
All right. I understand.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:24.110
Thank you for all you've done for me.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:29.110
I need to get my things together, 
so could you call my cousin Kuro?

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:31.620
Rikka-san.

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:36.300
Given your rather sudden discharge, 
do you have a place to stay?

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.500
Not yet.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.250
What?

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:41.210
Let me stay at your place for a while.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:46.530
You can't! My place is really small!

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:47.470
I can't?

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:51.300
I'll do the housework for you.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:54.210
House... work...?

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:56.730
Welcome home, Kuro.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.270
Your bath is ready.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.250
Goodnight.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:09.870
Did I say something strange?

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:13.380
No! But, I mean... I only have one bed...

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:15.070
Well, you do live on your own.

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.190
Wh-Which is exactly why...

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:21.590
I know! I'll talk to Iwanaga about it.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:23.410
Iwanaga's parents know a lot of people,

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:25.380
so they might be able to think of something.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.270
You don't have to go through all that.

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:30.630
If I can't stay at your place, 
I could always stay in a park...

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.340
Iwanaga? There's something 
I want to talk to you about.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:38.420
Kuro-san! What is it? It's unusual 
for you to turn to me for help.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:39.560
<i>You see—</i>

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:39.560
Wait.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:45.240
<i>Allow me to charge you a consultation fee.</i>

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:49.360
Really? The Goddess of Wisdom is 
going to charge a consultation fee?

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:54.460
Indeed. Depending on the client, 
I'd prefer favors or offerings over cash.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:56.200
I won't be asking for much.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.950
But this discussion might involve you, too...

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.420
Kuro-san, where are you right now?

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:07.420
The special lecture you wanted to attend 
at the university is happening right now.

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:13.270
<i>Yet you're contacting me and 
asking me for something.</i>

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:14.800
<i>This is no ordinary matter.</i>

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.070
<i>It is now 5:00 PM.</i>

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.430
And that very familiar recording 
I hear over the phone...

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:21.800
You're at the hospital right now.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.560
Which means that this has to do

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:25.490
<i>with Rikka-san.</i>

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:31.030
<i>So I should be allowed to be 
a bit forceful about this.</i>

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:36.320
Fear not. I wouldn't ask 
for anything too difficult.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:39.540
Let's hear the conditions.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.160
Let me have the spare key to your apartment.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:44.590
Don't be ridiculous.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.820
What's ridiculous about your 
girlfriend asking for the spare key

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.040
to your apartment?!

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:51.510
It's not like I plan to do anything bad.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:54.880
<i>Wouldn't it be lovely to have your 
girlfriend do your housework</i>

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.030
and welcome you home?

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.100
House... work...?

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:01.900
Welcome home!

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:04.930
I didn't cut any corners preparing 
your meals or your bed!

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:07.500
Bathing together! Bathing together!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.190
Sleeping together! Sleeping together!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:14.340
Kuro! I found a nice place to stay.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:15.130
Huh?!

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.410
Steamy

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.410
<b>Napping rooms available!!</b>

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.410
<b>Health Land</b>

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:17.410
<b>~The biggest bathhouse in the world~</b>

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:17.410
Here it is.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:23.480
<i>Okay. I'll give you my key, so help me out.</i>

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:24.830
This makes me so happy.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:27.940
At last, I'm your common-law wife!

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:29.330
<i>Yeah, no.</i>

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:32.840
And so I went to pick them up immediately,

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:35.610
and Rikka-san left the hospital behind.

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:38.720
So, yes...

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:42.860
We had plenty of vacant rooms 
at my house, so I welcomed her.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:45.280
I mean, she was a mysterious 
patient who had been

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:46.810
in the hospital for five years.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.700
So after she left, rumors spread 
that she had passed away.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:53.230
<i>And those rumors somehow reached me?</i>

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.040
In reality, she was doing rather well.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:59.240
Rikka-san is quite beautiful 
and very well-mannered,

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.580
so my aunt welcomed her with open arms.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.230
So Rikka-san didn't hate you?

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:07.700
Why do you just assume she hated me?

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:13.140
When I first met Rikka-san...

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:19.720
Kuro, I don't think she's 
a good match for you.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.000
I completely agree!

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:26.980
Huh?

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.990
That's cringe-worthy.

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:31.730
Yes. We all cringed.

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:35.360
Rikka-san even tried to remedy the situation.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.100
I mean, she's not good for you,

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.990
but she might not be the 
worst for you, either.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:41.790
You actually made Rikka-san feel bad?

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:43.820
You bet I did.

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:47.170
After that, we made up, and occasionally
went out together without Kuro-senpai.

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:50.640
We would even throw birthday parties 
for each other—with cake, of course!

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:51.710
Just the two of you?!

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.990
Happy birthday!

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:56.760
Thank you!

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.470
Yay!

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:02.300
Then what's she up to now?

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.060
You said she was at your place 
until a month ago, right?

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.110
We don't know where she is right now.

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:07.770
Huh?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:11.860
A month ago, she told my parents 
that she had officially found

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:15.010
a job and a place to stay, and she left.

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:17.100
We couldn't contact her on her cell,

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:20.130
and the new address and workplace 
she'd given us were fake.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.220
What did Kuro-kun do after he heard that?

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:26.460
Senpai went berserk and pushed me down...

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.910
Then, as if to vent his 
frustrations, he forcefully...

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:30.660
Answer the question seriously.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:37.500
Nothing, at first. He just said that 
Rikka-san probably had something in mind.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:41.130
But two weeks later, he started trying 
to get a hold of her repeatedly,

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.290
then he sent me a single 
message and disappeared.

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:45.150
Kuro-senpai

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:45.150
no subject

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:45.150
Something came up. Don't look for me.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:48.100
So, Saki-san, what's bothering you?

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:52.250
What did you and Senpai talk 
about while I was asleep?

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:58.110
I guess it didn't take you long to realize that 
Rikka-san was behind Steel Lady Nanase.

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:02.110
Kuro-kun didn't come here 
because you called him.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:04.420
He was looking for Rikka-san.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:09.590
<i>Something must've gotten them 
to talk about Rikka-san.</i>

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:12.830
<i>Not that I really care that she found out.</i>

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:16.090
<i>So nothing happened between them.</i>

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:18.340
<i>I can relax, then.</i>

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.610
Why did you hide it from me?

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:23.340
Because I didn't have any proof.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:28.650
Even when she was at my place, 
Rikka-san would mess with the computer,

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:31.100
but I never actually looked 
at what she was doing.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:33.510
I never would've thought that she was

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:37.980
creating a wiki page and bringing 
Steel Lady Nanase to life.

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:41.290
And I didn't really know 
about Steel Lady Nanase

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:44.360
until the monsters came to talk to me.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.370
I only realized that Rikka-san 
was involved when I saw

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:51.590
the picture on the wiki page I'd 
found when doing some research.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.660
Picture? You mean the picture 
that's on the main page?

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.260
Yes, precisely.

00:12:57.260 --> 00:13:00.960
It was painted in Rikka-san's style.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:10.970
She Who Spins Fiction

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.350
I believe it was about a year ago...

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.780
She suddenly became very 
serious about painting.

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:22.400
Looking back on it now,

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.660
I believe Rikka-san intended to create

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:27.030
a monster of the 
imagination even back then.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.550
In order to consolidate 
hundreds of thousands

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:34.290
of fantasies and give them a shared vision 
of a monster, name and shape are key.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:38.360
The most effective way would be to 
illustrate the story with a picture.

00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:42.300
When shown it, everyone would 
have the same image in mind.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:47.930
I'm sure Nanase Karin's accident 
gave her the perfect material.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.000
Though only known to some, 
she was still an idol in the public eye.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:51.120
<b>Nanase Karin's True Form</b>

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.310
She was involved in a dark scandal 
and died a very dramatic death.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.470
Add a ghost to the mix,

00:13:56.470 --> 00:14:00.250
and it has ample opportunity to 
evolve into a yokai or urban legend.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:03.260
There might've already been rumors

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:07.980
of the ghost of Nanase Karin 
appearing in Makurazaka City,

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:10.190
but the one who amplified them was Rikka-san.

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:15.330
I'm assuming the one who gave her 
the name "Steel Lady Nanase"

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:19.960
and made up the accompanying 
stories was also Rikka-san.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.710
Kuro-senpai realized this, too.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:25.260
While he was looking for Rikka-san,

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:28.970
he heard rumors about Steel Lady Nanase 
and sensed something.

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:31.650
And after he saw the picture on 
the Steel Lady Nanase wiki page,

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:33.970
he knew for sure, and so he came here.

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:35.690
Saki-san,

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:39.310
you're someone who decided to live 
your life seeing only the real world.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:42.230
What will you do now that you 
know what lies in the shadows?

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:44.480
Kuro-senpai probably

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:48.250
didn't tell you because he didn't 
want to further involve you in this.

00:14:48.890 --> 00:14:50.030
I see.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:53.640
Because Rikka-san, who has the 
same kudan ability to control

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:56.200
the future that Kuro-kun does, 
was pulling the strings,

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:59.290
Steel Lady Nanase was able 
to mature this quickly.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:00.890
That's very likely.

00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:04.540
Rikka-san probably died over 
and over to get the future where

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:07.430
people on the Internet wouldn't stop 
talking about Steel Lady Nanase,

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:09.510
and came back to life.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:11.940
But why would she do that?

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:16.140
What good comes out of creating a 
monster that will kill indiscriminately?

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:18.940
She has the power to determine the future,

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:21.100
but it's actually not all that impressive.

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:24.020
Kuro-senpai says that, too.

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:28.310
He can only choose a future that's 
within the scope of his own talents,

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:30.440
potential, and effort.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.250
Meaning he's not that different 
from a normal person.

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:36.080
But she successfully created a monster.

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:38.950
She's probably trying to find out

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:42.860
how far she can go with her 
ability to decide the future.

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:46.570
